WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:10.319
Ally delivered the huevos rancheros to the woman and then ducked into the kitchen, trying not to panic.

2
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:19.310
But the customer had seen her levitation ability!

3
00:00:19.311 --> 00:00:24.703
And now the woman was typing rapidly into her comm device!

4
00:00:24.704 --> 00:00:28.273
"What if she's one of those alien hunters?" Ally thought.

5
00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:33.339
"She might try to trap me and put me in the Sandville UFO Museum!"

6
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:39.122
Ally peeked out, watching the woman as she took a few bites of food and then put her fork down.

7
00:00:39.123 --> 00:00:46.587
She typed some more, casting her eyes all around the diner every once in a while.

8
00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:58.123
Ally was trying to read the woman's mind when a couple entered the diner.

9
00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:05.092
Ally sighed and went out to greet them.

10
00:01:05.093 --> 00:01:08.654
"Do you have room for us?" the woman asked.

11
00:01:08.655 --> 00:01:13.656
Ally gestured around the nearly empty diner. "We sure do."

12
00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:17.415
"Great!" the man said. "There are 12 of us."

13
00:01:17.416 --> 00:01:21.574
Ally's eyes went wide. "Twelve?"

14
00:01:21.575 --> 00:01:25.966
"We went to Pepe's first, but they said it would be a long wait."

15
00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:33.663
"Oh! Well, sit wherever you like, and I'll be right back to take your orders."

16
00:01:33.664 --> 00:01:45.367
Ally scurried to the office. "Ray!" she squealed. "Twelve people just walked in!"

17
00:01:45.368 --> 00:01:51.769
When she returned to the dining room with water for the new customers, they were chattering away to one another.

18
00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:55.263
". . . lecture on extraterrestrial life-forms . . ."

19
00:01:55.264 --> 00:01:58.674
". . . the foremost authority on other galaxies . . ."

20
00:01:58.675 --> 00:02:03.317
"No one knows more about the study of aliens . . ."

21
00:02:03.318 --> 00:02:07.657
"They're talking about that alien expert," Ally realized.

22
00:02:07.658 --> 00:02:13.825
Her heart sank. These customers must be alien hunters too!

23
00:02:13.826 --> 00:02:20.548
Then to Ally's horror, the woman in the leopard-print dress stood up and approached some people in the group.

24
00:02:20.549 --> 00:02:24.627
Ally dashed back into the kitchen.

25
00:02:24.628 --> 00:02:29.333
"She's telling them she saw me levitate that plate!" Ally thought.

26
00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:33.690
"Oh no. . . . What if they tell Dr. Lloyd about me?"

27
00:02:33.691 --> 00:02:36.943
She closed her eyes for a second, thinking about running away.

28
00:02:36.944 --> 00:02:41.117
But then her eyes landed on Ray, who was heating up a grill.

29
00:02:41.118 --> 00:02:44.147
"I can't abandon Ray," she thought.

30
00:02:44.148 --> 00:02:47.190
"And an Astralian never gives up.

31
00:02:47.191 --> 00:02:57.625
If the woman tells people she thinks I'm an alien, I'll just deny it! Ray will defend me!"

32
00:02:57.626 --> 00:03:06.396
When Ally went to take the new customers' orders, the woman in the leopard-print dress was gone.

33
00:03:06.397 --> 00:03:10.612
Ally took a deep breath.

34
00:03:10.613 --> 00:03:12.925
"What would you like?" she asked.

35
00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:17.060
"I'll have huevos rancheros," the first diner said.

36
00:03:17.061 --> 00:03:18.821
"Me too!"

37
00:03:18.822 --> 00:03:21.760
"Me three!"

38
00:03:21.761 --> 00:03:26.853
"We all want huevos rancheros," the first diner said.

39
00:03:26.854 --> 00:03:29.598
"Everyone?" Ally asked.

40
00:03:29.599 --> 00:03:32.383
"Yes!" the man went on.

41
00:03:32.384 --> 00:03:35.390
"Another customer was raving about them.

42
00:03:35.391 --> 00:03:38.814
She told us they couldn't be missed."

43
00:03:38.815 --> 00:03:44.278
"Is that all the woman was telling them?" Ally thought. "I hope so."

44
00:03:44.279 --> 00:03:55.347
"Twelve orders of huevos rancheros coming right up!" She rushed to the kitchen.

45
00:03:55.348 --> 00:04:01.459
Exactly one hour later, 12 satisfied customers filed out of the diner.

46
00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.993
None of them seemed to suspect a thing about Ally.

47
00:04:03.994 --> 00:04:08.530
And they all promised to come back with their friends and families soon.

48
00:04:08.531 --> 00:04:12.223
Ally blew out a breath.

49
00:04:12.224 --> 00:04:16.738
"If even half of them come back," she murmured,

50
00:04:16.739 --> 00:04:24.212
"and bring about two people with them, and then those two people return and bring two more, that's—"

51
00:04:24.213 --> 00:04:30.633
"Oh good!" Mateo rushed into the diner. "She's not here yet."

52
00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.955
"Who?" Ally asked.

53
00:04:32.956 --> 00:04:37.736
"It's no big deal," Mateo tried to sound casual.

54
00:04:37.737 --> 00:04:42.841
"Bethany's going to swing by to hang out."

55
00:04:42.842 --> 00:04:49.422
"Swing by to hang out?" Ally gazed up at the ceiling.

56
00:04:49.423 --> 00:04:53.540
Were they going to hang from the light fixtures or something?

57
00:04:53.541 --> 00:04:58.486
"Yeah, you know, to talk and have a bite to eat."

58
00:04:58.487 --> 00:05:03.436
"Oh!" Ally exclaimed. She shook her head.

59
00:05:03.437 --> 00:05:07.673
She would never get used to the weird things humans said.

60
00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:11.913
"And I have you to thank for it, Ally," Mateo went on.

61
00:05:11.914 --> 00:05:18.167
"If you hadn't said what you said, I'd never have gotten up the nerve to text Bethany."

62
00:05:18.168 --> 00:05:25.207
Ally tossed her hair proudly. "I like to do good deeds."

63
00:05:25.208 --> 00:05:30.684
By the time Bethany and Kate arrived, Ally felt herself relaxing—just a little.

64
00:05:30.685 --> 00:05:38.062
The customer in the leopard-print dress had just been telling the other customers about Ray's good food. That was all.

65
00:05:38.063 --> 00:05:42.345
"You've got nothing to worry about," she told herself firmly.

66
00:05:42.346 --> 00:05:45.282
"Except new parts and fuel."

67
00:05:45.283 --> 00:05:50.273
A second later a mother and daughter entered.

68
00:05:50.274 --> 00:05:54.325
"Two muffins to go, please," the mother said.

69
00:05:54.326 --> 00:06:02.492
As Ally handed the muffins to the woman, the little girl peered at her.

70
00:06:02.493 --> 00:06:07.914
"Look, Mommy! It's that alien from the park!"

